{title: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley (1739), alt. George Whitefield (1753)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune MENDELSSOHN - Felix Mendelssohn (1840), adapt. William H. Cummings (1856) (1856)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1753, tune 1856: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hark! the herald [D]angels [G]sing, "Glory [C]to the [G]new-born [D]King;
[G]Peace on earth, and [D]mercy [G]mild, God and [D]sinners [A]recon[D]ciled!"
[G]Joyful, all ye [C]nations, [D]rise, [G]join the [C]triumph [D]of the skies;
[C]With th'angelic [Am]host pro[D]claim, "Christ is [G]born in [D]Bethle[G]hem!"
[C]Hark! the herald [Am]angels [D]sing, "Glory [G]to the [D]new-born [G]King."
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Christ, by highest [D]heaven a[G]dored; Christ the [C]ever[G]lasting [D]Lord!
[G]Late in time be[D]hold Him [G]come, offspring [D]of a [A]virgin's [D]womb.
[G]Veiled in flesh the [C]Godhead [D]see; [G]hail the [C]incarnate [D]Deity,
[C]Pleased as man with [Am]men to [D]dwell, Jesus, [G]our Em[D]manu[G]el.
[C]Hark! the herald [Am]angels [D]sing, "Glory [G]to the [D]new-born [G]King."
{end_of_verse}
